# 低频词汇 List08
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2026恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List08核心词汇

milestone /ˈmaɪlstəʊn/ n. 里程碑 The invention was a milestone in communication technology. 该发明是通信技术的里程碑。
mislead /ˌmɪsˈliːd/ v. 误导 Statistics can be used to mislead the public. 统计数据可以被用来误导公众。
mobilize /ˈməʊbɪlaɪz/ v. 动员 The government mobilized resources for the disaster response. 政府动员了灾害应对资源。
monopoly /məˈnɒpəli/ n. 垄断 The company held a monopoly in the market for decades. 该公司在市场上垄断了几十年。
morale /məˈrɑːl/ n. 士气 Team morale improved after the success. 成功后团队士气提高了。
municipality /mjuːˌnɪsɪˈpæləti/ n. 市政府 The municipality approved the zoning change. 市政府批准了分区变更。
narrative /ˈnærətɪv/ n. 叙述 The dominant narrative has been challenged. 主流叙述受到了挑战。
necessitate /nəˈsesɪteɪt/ v. 使成为必要 The situation necessitates immediate action. 这种情况需要立即采取行动。
negligence /ˈneɡlɪdʒəns/ n. 疏忽 The accident was caused by professional negligence. 事故是由专业疏忽造成的。
nominee /ˌnɒmɪˈniː/ n. 被提名者 The nominee for the award is a renowned scientist. 该奖项的被提名者是一位著名科学家。
notorious /nəʊˈtɔːriəs/ adj. 臭名昭著的 The highway is notorious for accidents. 这条高速公路因事故而臭名昭著。
obsolete /ˈɒbsəliːt/ adj. 过时的 The old software has become obsolete. 旧软件已经过时了。
ominous /ˈɒmɪnəs/ adj. 不祥的 There are ominous signs of a coming recession. 有经济衰退即将到来的不祥征兆。
onset /ˈɒnset/ n. 发作 The onset of symptoms was sudden. 症状的发作很突然。
oppress /əˈpres/ v. 压迫 The regime systematically oppressed its citizens. 该政权系统性地压迫其公民。
oscillate /ˈɒsɪleɪt/ v. 摇摆 The market has oscillated between gains and losses. 市场在涨跌之间摇摆。
outbreak /ˈaʊtbreɪk/ n. 爆发 The outbreak of the virus caught the world by surprise. 病毒的爆发让世界措手不及。
outcry /ˈaʊtkraɪ/ n. 抗议 The decision provoked a public outcry. 该决定引发了公众的强烈抗议。
outskirts /ˈaʊtskɜːts/ n. 郊区 The factory is located on the outskirts of the city. 工厂位于城市郊区。
overhaul /ˌəʊvəˈhɔːl/ v./n. 全面改革 The tax system is in need of a complete overhaul. 税制需要全面改革。
overt /əʊˈvɜːt/ adj. 公开的 There was no overt sign of conflict. 没有公开的冲突迹象。
overthrow /ˌəʊvəˈθrəʊ/ v./n. 推翻 The revolution overthrew the authoritarian regime. 革命推翻了独裁政权。
overwhelm /ˌəʊvəˈwelm/ v. 压垮 The volume of applications overwhelmed the system. 大量的申请压垮了系统。
oxide /ˈɒksaɪd/ n. 氧化物 Nitrogen oxide contributes to air pollution. 氮氧化物加剧了空气污染。
pact /pækt/ n. 协议 The two nations signed a non-aggression pact. 两国签署了一项互不侵犯协议。
pandemic /pænˈdemɪk/ n. 大流行病 The pandemic caused unprecedented disruption. 大流行病造成了前所未有的破坏。
paradox /ˈpærədɒks/ n. 矛盾 It is a paradox that technology both connects and isolates us. 技术既连接又孤立我们，这是一个矛盾。
paralyze /ˈpærəlaɪz/ v. 使瘫痪 The strike paralyzed the city's transport network. 罢工使城市交通网络瘫痪。
patron /ˈpeɪtrən/ n. 赞助人 The museum's patrons include several wealthy donors. 博物馆的赞助人包括几位富有的捐赠者。
peculiar /pɪˈkjuːliə(r)/ adj. 特有的 The region has its own peculiar customs. 该地区有其特有的习俗。
